      "title": "Helen Haines live updates: MP critical but stable as AFP look into charges carrying up to 10 years’ imprisonment",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/20/helen-haines-independent-mp-alleged-car-attack-wangaratta-melbourne-hospital-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>A joint counter-terrorism taskforce is investigating the incident, which Anthony Albanese alleged ‘wasn’t an accident’</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/19/mp-helen-haines-injured-incident-wangaratta-ntwnfb\">‘Deeply appalled’: politicians condemn alleged attack after Helen Haines critically injured</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/19/who-is-helen-haines-the-mp-allegedly-attacked-in-victoria-ntwnfb\">Helen Haines, the principled MP respected across parliament</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>‘It’s very clear that this was a deliberate act’, PM says</strong></p><p>The prime minister, <strong>Anthony Albanese</strong>, said Haines’ alleged attacker “did a U-turn in order to get back to where <strong>Helen Haines</strong> was” after passing her on the road.</p><p>It would appear that the driver of the vehicle that inflicted the damage to Helen Haines did a U-turn in order to get back to where Helen Haines was after passing where she was getting things from the boot or putting things into the boot of her car.</p><p>So it’s clear that there was a deliberate act here, this wasn’t an accident – someone, you know, just getting off the road here.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/20/helen-haines-independent-mp-alleged-car-attack-wangaratta-melbourne-hospital-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-20T02:02:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Kumanjayi Little Baby: damning report finds ‘heartbreaking’ child protection failures before five-year-old’s death",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/20/kumanjayi-little-baby-damning-report-finds-heartbreaking-child-protection-failures-before-five-year-olds-death-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Northern Territory government announced sweeping reforms of child protection sector in May, just days after the Warlpiri girl was found dead</p><p><em><strong>• Warning: </strong>This article contains images of and references to Indigenous Australians who have died</em></p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A report into the Northern Territory’s child protection sector has detailed “confronting” and “heartbreaking” failures in the lead-up to the alleged murder of Warlpiri girl Kumanjayi Little Baby.</p><p>The five-year-old was found dead in April, five days after she was allegedly abducted from a town camp in Alice Springs.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/20/kumanjayi-little-baby-damning-report-finds-heartbreaking-child-protection-failures-before-five-year-olds-death-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-20T01:50:49"
    },
    {
      "title": "Car allegedly did U-turn and struck Helen Haines twice, in what some believe was targeted attack against MP",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/20/helen-haines-mp-alleged-attack-wangaratta-surgery-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Independent MP is in critical yet stable condition, as police interview alleged attacker in Wangaratta incident</p><ul><li><p>Follow our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/20/helen-haines-independent-mp-alleged-car-attack-wangaratta-melbourne-hospital-ntwnfb\">Helen Haines live blog</a> for latest updates</p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/19/who-is-helen-haines-the-mp-allegedly-attacked-in-victoria-ntwnfb\">Who is Helen Haines, the MP allegedly attacked in Victoria?</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The man accused of attacking Helen Haines allegedly made a U-turn before ramming the independent MP twice in what some believed may be a targeted attack near her electorate office, according to eyewitnesses.</p><p>The independent MP remains in a critical condition after being airlifted from Wangaratta in northern Victoria to Melbourne’s Alfred hospital for emergency surgery on Monday night.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/20/helen-haines-mp-alleged-attack-wangaratta-surgery-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-20T01:50:34"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘I don’t want to be known as a hero’: barber who rushed to help Helen Haines praised by PM",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/20/i-dont-want-to-be-known-as-a-hero-barber-who-rushed-to-help-helen-haines-praised-by-pm-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Ricky Jefferies says he had just finished cutting hair when he grabbed and held the driver who allegedly deliberately struck the Indi MP</p><ul><li><p>Follow our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/20/helen-haines-independent-mp-alleged-car-attack-wangaratta-melbourne-hospital-ntwnfb\">Helen Haines live blog</a> for latest updates</p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/19/who-is-helen-haines-the-mp-allegedly-attacked-in-victoria-ntwnfb\">Who is Helen Haines, the MP allegedly attacked in Victoria?</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Australian prime minister has hailed him a hero for rushing out of his shop to help independent MP Helen Haines after she was allegedly run down in a deliberate attack – but barber Ricky Jefferies says he had “no choice” but to intervene.</p><p>Standing on Tuesday morning outside his shop, which is right next to Haines’ electorate office in Wangaratta, Jefferies was almost shy about the whole thing.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/20/i-dont-want-to-be-known-as-a-hero-barber-who-rushed-to-help-helen-haines-praised-by-pm-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-20T01:49:55"
    },
    {
